		{
			dependencies: ["156007E8F6D5F7E3", "315D139892728739"]
			description: [
				"Use a Training Treat to turn a wolf into a trained dog, then open its interface and learn the core stats. Talents specialise the companion; they are not all useful for every owner's play style."
				"Dogs use nourishment and need suitable food. A Food Bowl can anchor wandering behaviour and provide a reliable home routine, while movement modes decide whether the dog follows, stays or patrols."
				"Start with survivability and control before combat talents. A companion that reliably returns and eats is more valuable than one with damage points nobody can safely command."
			]
			id: "36972E6369FFABEA"
			rewards: [{
				id: "0B5D66E03FC6C4F9"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "A trained dog has nourishment, modes and a job"
			tasks: [{
				id: "07FF853A6E6004CF"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Doggy Talents Next"
			x: 6.0d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["36972E6369FFABEA"]
			description: [
				"Domestication Innovation expands pet equipment, control and protection. Use its beds, tags and command tools to make companions recoverable and recognisable."
				"Keep dangerous pets out of public doorways and farms, and test interaction settings before bringing them into a boss fight. Multiplayer pets need names and owners everyone can identify."
				"Create a safe home area with food, storage and written instructions. If another player cannot tell whether a pet should follow them, the setup is unfinished."
				"Domestication Innovation supports safer long-term pets with equipment and behaviour improvements. Name important companions, provide home positions, and do not test teleportation or combat settings for the first time inside a dimension portal."
			]
			id: "67FACF25579F11E0"
			rewards: [{
